# Security headers for every address on the site (t22, 22 Nov 2026).
# Read by Cloudflare Workers static assets like _redirects; it is never served as a file itself.
# Limits: 100 rules, 2,000 characters a line. A header named in two matching rules is joined with a comma.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is deliberately NOT here: it is set in the Cloudflare dashboard
# (SSL/TLS > Edge Certificates > HSTS). Sending a second one from this file could disagree with it.
#
# Content-Security-Policy, in plain words:
#   script-src  : this site, inline <script> blocks and onclick handlers (the menu, the Black Friday
#                 strip, the support FAQ), and Cloudflare Web Analytics' beacon. 'unsafe-inline' is
#                 needed because the publisher rewrites pages, so per-script hashes would go stale.
#                 Cloudflare's own bot check is inline and loads from /cdn-cgi/ on this site.
#   connect-src : this site (/cdn-cgi/rum and the bot check) and Cloudflare Web Analytics.
#   img-src     : this site and data: (the hero tiles in site.css are a data: SVG).
#   style-src   : this site and inline <style> / style="".
#   everything else: this site only; no plugins, no <base> rewrite, forms post only here,
#   and no other site may put these pages in a frame.
# Before adding a third-party script, embed, font or image host to any page, add it here first.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
